# spike 03 bench, debug build

## Stack used per call that isn't a tail call

- command, then more: 2001 calls deep used 2751 KiB, 1408 bytes a call
- inside an expression: 2001 calls deep used 7440 KiB, 3809 bytes a call
- fib-style, two calls: 2001 calls deep used 7440 KiB, 3809 bytes a call
- inside REPEAT and IFELSE lists: 2001 calls deep used 10563 KiB, 5408 bytes a call

Worst case 5408 bytes a call, so a 256 MiB stack fits about 49588 calls.
Endless recursion through lists, no depth limit: stopped by the stack guard at 49590 calls: "DOWN called itself too many times: 49590 calls deep. Does it have a way to STOP?"

